      "model": "Model A",
      "style": "Story",
      "length": "Brief",
      "language": "中文",
      "sampleText": "When Mia moved to a small town, she did not know anyone. Each morning, she would wander through the quiet streets with a notebook in her pocket. She wrote down little things: a bright blue door, the smell of fresh bread, and the old man who watered flowers outside the library.\n\nOne rainy afternoon, Mia stepped into a bookshop. The owner noticed her notebook and invited her to join a writing group. Mia felt nervous, but she decided to share a page. Soon, other people began sharing their own memories. Together, they learned to weave ordinary moments into stories worth telling.\n\nNot every day was easy. Sometimes Mia missed her old home, yet she remained resilient. By the end of the month, the town no longer felt unfamiliar. She had found friends, a favorite bookshop, and a new story of her own.",
      "meanings": [
